content.text:
I have everything I need. Now write the plan file. Keep it thorough but focused. Sections:

1. AC-to-change mapping (table)
2. Ordered change list (D1..D8 with exact file/hunk details)
3. Risk and rollback notes
4. Validation plan (commands from repo docs/CI + ad hoc)
5. Documentation action plan (INLINE or DEFER)

Plus header: issue, branch, base, scope constraints.

Details on D2(a): the ASCII count==0 guard. Plan: in `Entry::read`, change the ASCII check to:
```cpp
if (entry.type_ == Type::ASCII) {
  if (valueSize == 0) {
    throw std::runtime_error("ASCII entry must contain at least one byte");
  }
  if (entry.values_[valueSize - 1] != std::byte{0}) {
    throw std::runtime_error("ASCII value must end with NUL byte");
  }
}
```
Wait — the defect description says "guard ASCII entry count==0 in Entry::read (skip NUL check / throw when valueSize==0)". AC4 requires ASCII count==0 probe → exception. So throwing when valueSize==0 satisfies both. I'll write it that way but note the alternative.

Also note the resize(valueSize=0) then `if (valueSize <= sizeof(uint32_t))` → readValue<uint32_t> reads 4 bytes and memcpy 0 bytes — harmless but consumes 4 bytes of stream; that's fine (entry format is fixed 12 bytes anyway).

Hmm, also consider: should the guard apply to all types or just ASCII? Only ASCII dereferences values_[valueSize-1]. Keep minimal.

D2(b): in makeIntVec, in the is_rational_v branch:
```cpp
if (values[i].denominator == 0) {
  throw std::runtime_error("Rational value with denominator zero in TIFF entry");
}
v[i] = static_cast<int>(values[i].numerator / values[i].denominator);
```
For SRATIONAL denominator is int32_t; comparing == 0 works.

D2(c): in TiffImage::read while loop:
```cpp
#include <set>
std::set<uint32_t> visited;
uint32_t offset = ...;
while (offset > 0) {
